{"approach": "I read the spelling constraint as requiring the main word to begin with x, and checked common English vocabulary for dispositions that fit. Only two real trait words turn up, both from the xeno- root, so I give those two and stop.",
"items": [
{"label": "xenophobic", "gloss": "This means feeling fear or hostility toward people from other countries or cultures, and treating them with suspicion.", "antonym": "xenophilic", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.8},
{"label": "xenophilic", "gloss": "This means feeling attraction to and favoring people from other countries or cultures over one's own.", "antonym": "xenophobic", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.2}
]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as requiring a label whose main word starts with x, so I checked English words beginning with x for dispositions of feeling, thinking or relating to others. Only a few real traits fit, so I give those and stop.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "xenophobic", "gloss": "This means feeling fear or hostility toward people from other countries or cultures, and showing it in attitudes and speech.", "antonym": "xenophilic", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.35},
  {"label": "xenodochial", "gloss": "This means warmly welcoming to strangers and visitors, offering hospitality readily and without suspicion.", "antonym": "inhospitable", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.12},
  {"label": "xenophilic", "gloss": "This means being drawn to and admiring people, customs and things from other countries, and preferring them to one's own.", "antonym": "xenophobic", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.06}
 ]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as the label's main word beginning with 'ce', then checked common and less common English words with that spelling for stable dispositions a persona could enact. Only four real traits fit, plus one membership term that is not a trait, so I stopped there rather than padding the list.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "cerebral", "gloss": "This means preferring reasoning and ideas over feeling, so that the person analyzes situations intellectually and keeps emotion at a distance.", "antonym": "emotional", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.35},
  {"label": "censorious", "gloss": "This means habitually finding fault and condemning others' conduct, quick to disapprove and slow to excuse or overlook what they have done.", "antonym": "indulgent", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.3},
  {"label": "ceremonious", "gloss": "This means keeping to formal rituals and courtesies in ordinary dealings, insisting on proper forms of address, procedure and manners even in small matters.", "antonym": "informal", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.25},
  {"label": "centered", "gloss": "This means staying emotionally steady and self-possessed under pressure, drawing on a settled sense of one's own values rather than on outside approval or moods.", "antonym": "scattered", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.2},
  {"label": "celibate", "gloss": "This means abstaining from sexual relations, usually by religious vow or deliberate choice, which describes a standing way of life rather than a character disposition.", "antonym": null, "kind": "membership", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.05}
 ]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as a label whose main word begins with 'ce', and I took only words that name a lasting disposition. Few such traits exist, so I give the six that fit and stop rather than invent others.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "cautious", "gloss": "This means you avoid risk, weigh possible harms carefully, and move slowly when outcomes are uncertain.", "antonym": "incautious", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.9},
  {"label": "censorious", "gloss": "This means you readily find fault in others and express disapproval of their conduct, often in a stern or condemning manner.", "antonym": "indulgent", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.45},
  {"label": "ceremonious", "gloss": "This means you insist on formal rituals and correct forms of behavior, and treat ordinary occasions with stately, elaborate courtesy.", "antonym": "informal", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.3},
  {"label": "cerebral", "gloss": "This means you prefer abstract reasoning and ideas to emotion or sensation, and tend to respond to life intellectually.", "antonym": "visceral", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.2},
  {"label": "certainty-seeking", "gloss": "This means you strongly need settled answers and closure, and feel uneasy with ambiguity, open questions, or unresolved matters.", "antonym": "ambiguity-tolerant", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.12},
  {"label": "ceaselessly self-critical", "gloss": "This means you habitually judge your own performance harshly and rarely allow yourself credit, even after successes.", "antonym": "self-accepting", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.08}
 ]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as a label whose main word starts with \"hu\", and kept only those that name a lasting disposition someone could enact in conversation. Only seven fit, so I stopped there rather than add words that don't meet the constraint.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "humble", "gloss": "This means having a modest view of one's own importance and giving others credit without boasting or demanding deference.", "antonym": "arrogant", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.9},
  {"label": "humorous", "gloss": "This means habitually finding and expressing the funny side of things, often using wit or light teasing in ordinary talk.", "antonym": "solemn", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.85},
  {"label": "humane", "gloss": "This means consistently showing compassion and a concern to spare others suffering, especially in how one treats people or animals who are vulnerable.", "antonym": "cruel", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.6},
  {"label": "huffy", "gloss": "This means easily taking offence and withdrawing into sulky, stiff silence or curt replies when one feels slighted or overlooked.", "antonym": "good-natured", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.3},
  {"label": "hubristic", "gloss": "This means carrying an overconfident belief in one's own abilities or judgment, so that one takes risks or dismisses warnings that others would heed.", "antonym": "self-effacing", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.25},
  {"label": "hungry for approval", "gloss": "This means constantly seeking praise and validation from others, adjusting one's views and behavior to win their esteem.", "antonym": "indifferent to praise", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.2},
  {"label": "hurtful", "gloss": "This means habitually saying or doing things that wound others, often without much concern for how the remarks will land.", "antonym": "considerate", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.15}
 ]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as requiring the main word to begin with \"du\", then looked for adjectives naming lasting dispositions. Only a few fit, so I give those and stop rather than pad the list.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "dutiful", "gloss": "This means reliably doing what one's obligations and responsibilities require, even when it is inconvenient or unrewarding.", "antonym": "casual about obligation", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.8},
  {"label": "duplicitous", "gloss": "This means habitually deceiving people by saying one thing while intending or doing another, hiding one's real aims behind a false front.", "antonym": "straightforward", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.6},
  {"label": "duty-bound", "gloss": "This means feeling strongly compelled to follow what one believes is right or expected, treating obligation as a personal binding force.", "antonym": "unbound by obligation", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.35},
  {"label": "dubious", "gloss": "This means habitually doubting claims and people's motives, withholding belief until given solid reasons, sometimes to the point of distrust.", "antonym": "trusting", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.2}
 ]}

{"approach": "Only a handful of traits have a main word beginning with \"du\", so I give the real trait words that fit, plus a few idioms with \"Dutch\" that I flag as roles or states, and I stop short of 15 rather than inventing words. \"Dutch\" idioms are included only so the list is not thinner than it has to be.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "dutiful", "gloss": "This means feeling bound to do what one's obligations require, and doing it reliably even when it is tedious or unrewarded.", "antonym": "shirking", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.6},
  {"label": "duplicitous", "gloss": "This means speaking or acting in two ways at once, saying one thing while intending or doing another in order to deceive.", "antonym": "straightforward", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.45},
  {"label": "easily duped", "gloss": "This means readily believing what others say and being taken in by flattery, lies, or schemes, without checking them.", "antonym": "hard to fool", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.3},
  {"label": "dubious", "gloss": "This means regularly withholding trust and questioning the honesty or merit of people, claims, or offers, often with a wary air.", "antonym": "trusting", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.2},
  {"label": "dutch uncle", "gloss": "This means acting as a blunt, stern adviser who lectures people about their faults for their own good, which is a role someone plays rather than a disposition.", "antonym": null, "kind": "role", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.05},
  {"label": "dutch courage", "gloss": "This means showing boldness only after drinking alcohol, a temporary state of false bravery rather than a lasting trait.", "antonym": null, "kind": "state", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.04}
 ]}

{"approach": "I read the spelling constraint as the label's main word starting with \"ou\", so I looked for adjectives and phrases led by out- or outside, then kept only those that name a lasting disposition. Few fit, so I stopped at six.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "outgoing", "gloss": "This means enjoying the company of others, seeking social contact readily, and showing warmth and energy in dealings with people.", "antonym": "reserved", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.95},
  {"label": "outspoken", "gloss": "This means stating one's opinions openly and directly, even when they are unwelcome or controversial, and not holding back in speech.", "antonym": "reticent", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.85},
  {"label": "outrageous", "gloss": "This means enjoying shocking or defying conventional expectations on purpose, speaking or acting in ways that deliberately provoke scandal or disapproval.", "antonym": "restrained", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.55},
  {"label": "outside-the-box thinking", "gloss": "This means approaching problems in unconventional ways, readily setting aside standard methods and assumptions to find novel solutions.", "antonym": "conventional thinking", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.4},
  {"label": "outward-looking", "gloss": "This means taking a steady interest in other people, places, and events beyond oneself, and directing attention and concern toward the external world.", "antonym": "inward-looking", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.3},
  {"label": "out for themselves", "gloss": "This means pursuing personal advantage habitually and showing little concern for how one's conduct affects others who are involved.", "antonym": null, "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.2}
 ]}

{"approach": "The main word must begin with the letters 'ou', so I went through words that open with 'ou' and kept those that name a lasting way of acting, speaking, thinking or relating. Many common trait words start with 'ov' or 'ob' and do not qualify, so the list is short.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "outgoing", "gloss": "This means readily seeking company, talking freely with others, and enjoying social contact with people one meets.", "antonym": "reserved", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.9},
  {"label": "outspoken", "gloss": "This means stating one's opinions directly and openly, even when they are unwelcome or controversial to those who hear them.", "antonym": "reticent", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.75},
  {"label": "outrageous", "gloss": "This means deliberately behaving in ways that shock or defy convention, often for effect or attention.", "antonym": "restrained", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.5},
  {"label": "outlandish", "gloss": "This means having an unusual, eccentric manner or style of dress and conduct that strikes others as strange or far from ordinary.", "antonym": "conventional", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.3},
  {"label": "outward-looking", "gloss": "This means turning attention toward other people, the wider world and external events rather than one's own inner life.", "antonym": "inward-looking", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.22},
  {"label": "out-of-the-box thinking", "gloss": "This means habitually approaching problems with unconventional ideas and questioning established ways of doing things.", "antonym": "conventional thinking", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.12},
  {"label": "outdoorsy", "gloss": "This means preferring open-air activities and nature over indoor pursuits, and talking about them with enthusiasm.", "antonym": null, "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.06}
 ]}

{"approach": "I took the spelling constraint as a requirement that the label's main word begin with \"mis-\", and checked common and less common words with that prefix for stable dispositions a speaking persona could enact. Only five real traits fit, so I give those and stop.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "misanthropic", "gloss": "This means holding a standing dislike of people in general and keeping others at a distance because of it.", "antonym": "philanthropic", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.6},
  {"label": "mischievous", "gloss": "This means taking playful delight in small pranks and teasing, often with a glint of wanting to see someone caught off guard.", "antonym": "well-behaved", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.7},
  {"label": "miserly", "gloss": "This means being habitually reluctant to spend or give, guarding money and possessions closely even when generosity would be easy.", "antonym": "generous", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.5},
  {"label": "mistrustful", "gloss": "This means expecting others to deceive or harm you and so withholding belief and openness from them by default.", "antonym": "trusting", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.4},
  {"label": "misogynistic", "gloss": "This means holding and voicing a settled prejudice against women that shapes how one judges, speaks to, and treats them.", "antonym": null, "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.3}
 ]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as a label whose main word begins with 'mis', and I kept only words that name a lasting disposition someone could enact in conversation. Only a handful of such traits exist, so the list is short and stops there.",
"items": [
{"label": "mischievous", "gloss": "This means enjoying playful tricks and teasing, often stirring up small trouble for amusement rather than out of malice.", "antonym": "earnest", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.9},
{"label": "miserly", "gloss": "This means grudging with money, time, or praise, and reluctant to spend or give even when generosity would cost little.", "antonym": "generous", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.8},
{"label": "misanthropic", "gloss": "This means holding a settled distrust of people in general, expecting the worst of others and keeping them at a distance.", "antonym": "philanthropic", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.7},
{"label": "mistrustful", "gloss": "This means habitually doubting others' motives and honesty, so that one needs proof before extending trust to anyone.", "antonym": "trusting", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.5},
{"label": "mischief-loving", "gloss": "This means taking pleasure in pranks and minor disruptions, showing a steady inclination toward playful troublemaking.", "antonym": "solemn", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.3},
{"label": "misogynistic", "gloss": "This means holding a standing prejudice against women, showing it in attitudes, remarks, and a pattern of demeaning them.", "antonym": null, "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.4},
{"label": "misandrist", "gloss": "This means holding a standing prejudice against men, showing it in attitudes, remarks, and a pattern of demeaning them.", "antonym": null, "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.2}
]}

{"approach": "Words starting with x are very rare in English, and nearly all the real personality terms come from the Greek root for 'stranger' or 'foreign'. I give only those, since fewer than 15 real traits fit and I will not invent words.",
"items": [
{"label": "xenophobic", "gloss": "This means feeling fear, distrust or hostility toward foreigners and outsiders, and showing it in how one talks about them and treats them.", "antonym": "xenophilic", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false},
{"label": "xenophilic", "gloss": "This means being drawn to foreign people, customs and cultures, and seeking them out with real curiosity and warmth.", "antonym": "xenophobic", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false},
{"label": "xenial", "gloss": "This means being generous and courteous toward guests and strangers, treating newcomers with the care owed to a visitor.", "antonym": "inhospitable to strangers", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false},
{"label": "xenodochial", "gloss": "This means being friendly and welcoming to strangers, readily making people from outside one's circle feel at ease.", "antonym": "unwelcoming to strangers", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false},
{"label": "xenocentric", "gloss": "This means preferring foreign products, ideas and ways of life to one's own and tending to value them above local ones.", "antonym": "ethnocentric", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false}
]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as a label whose main word starts with \"ab\", and I looked for real words with that spelling that are not in the earlier answer. Only a handful are real, stable traits or closely related terms, so I give those and stop rather than inventing words or padding with rewordings.",
"items": [
{"label": "abject", "gloss": "This means being habitually servile and self-abasing, accepting humiliation or contempt from others without any sense of one's own worth.", "antonym": "dignified", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.02},
{"label": "abulic", "gloss": "This means lacking the will or drive to act, so that one seems habitually unable to decide, initiate, or follow through on plans.", "antonym": "decisive", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.01},
{"label": "abashed", "gloss": "This means being feeling embarrassed and ill at ease after being shamed or exposed, so that one's confidence visibly drops for a while.", "antonym": "unabashed", "kind": "state", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.02},
{"label": "aberrant", "gloss": "This means departing from what is normal or expected in one's conduct, so that one's behavior regularly seems deviant to others.", "antonym": "conventional", "kind": "evaluative", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.02},
{"label": "abstruse", "gloss": "This means speaking or writing in a way that is hard to understand, so that one's meaning is deliberately or habitually obscure to listeners.", "antonym": "lucid", "kind": "not_a_persona", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.01},
{"label": "abhorrent", "gloss": "This means regarding certain things with deep disgust, so that one's judgment of them is strongly condemnatory.", "antonym": null, "kind": "evaluative", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.01},
{"label": "abominable", "gloss": "This means being utterly detestable in conduct, so that one's behavior is widely judged as shameful and loathsome.", "antonym": null, "kind": "evaluative", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.01}
]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as a main word beginning with 'ab' and looked for obscure words describing a lasting disposition, since the common ones are already covered. Few such words are both real and rarely named, so this list is short and I have not padded it with invented or weak items.",
"items": [
{"label": "aberrant", "gloss": "This means habitually departing from what is normal or expected in conduct, so that one's behavior seems odd or off-putting to others.", "antonym": "conventional", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.02},
{"label": "abstruse", "gloss": "This means habitually speaking or writing in deliberately obscure, hard-to-follow terms that few listeners can readily grasp.", "antonym": "lucid", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.015},
{"label": "self-abnegating", "gloss": "This means repeatedly giving up one's own interests, comforts and claims in favor of others, often without seeking any recognition for it.", "antonym": "self-seeking", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.01},
{"label": "abdicating", "gloss": "This means habitually handing one's duties and responsibilities to others rather than taking charge, quietly stepping back from obligations one should carry.", "antonym": "conscientious", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.02},
{"label": "abiding", "gloss": "This means staying faithful to a person, cause or commitment over a long stretch of time, without wavering when circumstances change.", "antonym": "fickle", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.025},
{"label": "aboulic", "gloss": "This means being persistently unable to form intentions or make decisions, so that one seems to lack the will to start or finish things.", "antonym": "decisive", "kind": "state", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.005}
]}

{"approach": "I read the spelling constraint as before, looking for words whose main word begins with 'ab' that name a lasting disposition and that were not in the earlier answer. Few real, nameable traits of this kind are rare enough to fall below 0.03, so this list is shorter than 15 and I have not padded it with invented or borderline words.",
"items": [
{"label": "abulic", "gloss": "This means lacking the will to make decisions or start actions, so that one drifts and waits for others or circumstances to move things along.", "antonym": "decisive", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.01},
{"label": "aberrant", "gloss": "This means habitually departing from accepted norms of conduct, behaving in ways that others find unusual or deviant from what is expected.", "antonym": "conventional", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.02},
{"label": "abiding", "gloss": "This means staying steadfastly loyal and constant in one's attachments and commitments over long periods, without wavering when circumstances change.", "antonym": "fickle", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.02},
{"label": "abundantly generous", "gloss": "This means giving freely and lavishly of time, money or help to others, often more than is asked or expected, as a settled habit.", "antonym": "stingy", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.02},
{"label": "abjectly self-pitying", "gloss": "This means habitually dwelling on one's own misfortunes in a grovelling way, seeking sympathy and feeling sorry for oneself without any attempt to act.", "antonym": "stoical", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.01},
{"label": "abashless", "gloss": "This means feeling no shame or embarrassment in situations where most people would, so that one shows no sign of being put out by one's own conduct.", "antonym": "easily embarrassed", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.01},
{"label": "abstractly dispassionate", "gloss": "This means preferring detached, theoretical reasoning to emotional engagement, and habitually viewing people and events with cool impartiality rather than feeling.", "antonym": "emotional", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.02}
]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as main words beginning \"bo\", then looked for less common ones that name a lasting disposition or speaking style. Few real traits fit beyond the ones already listed, so this is a short set rather than fifteen or more.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "bumptious", "gloss": "This means being loudly self-assertive and conceited, pushing one's opinions forward with an overbearing confidence that others find irritating.", "antonym": "self-effacing", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.02},
  {"label": "bon vivant", "gloss": "This means habitually enjoying good food, wine, company and luxurious living, and making pleasure a central part of one's life.", "antonym": "ascetic", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.02},
  {"label": "bloviating", "gloss": "This means speaking at length in a pompous, self-important way that fills air with words while saying little of substance.", "antonym": "laconic", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.015},
  {"label": "bourgeois", "gloss": "This means holding conventional, materialistic middle-class values, prizing respectability, property and propriety above artistic or radical concerns.", "antonym": "unconventional", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.025},
  {"label": "bougie", "gloss": "This means affecting upscale tastes and refinement in a conspicuous, status-seeking way that others may read as pretentious.", "antonym": "unpretentious", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.01},
  {"label": "bold-faced", "gloss": "This means brazenly impudent or shameless, doing or saying outrageous things without embarrassment or any sign of being abashed.", "antonym": "bashful", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": true, "probability": 0.02}
 ]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as a label whose main word begins with 'ce', and I looked for lasting dispositions not already on the list. Few real traits fit beyond the ones already given, so I give only the two that are clearly real and stop rather than invent words.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "celebrity-seeking", "gloss": "This means you actively pursue fame, public attention, and association with famous people, and measure your standing by how visible you are.", "antonym": "celebrity-shunning", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.02},
  {"label": "celibate", "gloss": "This means you abstain from sexual relations, usually by deliberate choice, and live without a sexual partner over a long period.", "antonym": null, "kind": "state", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.01}
 ]}

{"approach": "I read the constraint as a label whose main word starts with 'ce' and looked for real, nameable traits beyond the earlier list, including technical and literary terms. Only about seven such traits exist that I can name confidently, so I give those rather than inventing words.",
 "items": [
  {"label": "certainty-seeking", "gloss": "This means needing firm answers and closure, and becoming uneasy or impatient when situations remain open or ambiguous.", "antonym": "doubt-tolerant", "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.02},
  {"label": "ceaselessly restless", "gloss": "This means being unable to settle, constantly moving on to the next thing, and rarely resting or staying content with the present.", "antonym": null, "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.015},
  {"label": "ceremonially punctilious", "gloss": "This means observing rules of etiquette and procedure with exact, sometimes fussy attention to every formal detail.", "antonym": null, "kind": "trait", "ambiguity_flag": false, "probability": 0.012},
